theorem a-row-multiplied-by-a-negative-number-read-from-its-other-side
  note        Multiplying 4·x − 5 ≤ 0 by −2 turns the relation round, to
              −8·x + 10 ≥ 0, and a restate row reads that order from its
              other side, 0 ≤ −8·x + 10.
  let x ∈ ℝ                                                           (H1)
  assume 4·x − 5 ≤ 0                                                  (H2)
  then 0 ≤ −8·x + 10

1.  0 ≤ −8·x + 10
    inequalities
      4·x − 5 ≤ 0        H2
      −8·x + 10 ≥ 0      multiplying by −2
      0 ≤ −8·x + 10      restate
